│ findings suggest that the recommended practice of individual health education for postnatal mothers in poor          │
│ communities has no impact on infant feeding, care, or immunisation, although uptake of family planning may be        │
│ slightly enhanced."}, {"study_index": 6, "title": "Impact of packaged interventions on neonatal health: a review of  │
│ the evidence", "abstract": "A disproportionate burden of infant and under-five childhood mortality occurs during the │
